WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.240
- [Instructor] We're told we know

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:04.000
that five times three is equal to 15.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.230
Yep, that's true.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:08.430
So which of the following
statements are also true?

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.870
And it says to choose two answers.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:14.550
So pause this video and see
if you can work through that.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.760
All right, now let's go
through them one by one.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.510
So this first one says,
"Three is a multiple of 15."

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.300
Now, in order for three to be
able to be a multiple of 15,

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.280
that means that we can multiply 15

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.600
by some whole number to get to three.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:32.040
But a multiple of 15,
we're thinking 15, 30, 45,

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.370
it's not gonna be three.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.600
What whole number can I
multiple 15 by to get three?

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.470
If I multiply 15 by
one, I'm already at 15.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:40.330
So this is not going to be our choice.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:42.710
And since it say pick two answers, well,

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.440
we might be able to figure out it's these.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.750
But let's just read them

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.710
to make sure that they make sense.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:49.790
15 is a multiple of three.

00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:52.690
So that means I can multiply
three times some whole number

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.170
to get to 15, and we know
what that whole number is.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:56.003
It's five.

00:00:56.003 --> 00:00:56.836
They tell us right over there.

00:00:56.836 --> 00:00:58.730
Five times three is 15.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:02.250
So 15 is a multiple of three.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.310
15 would also be a multiple
of five 'cause I can

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:06.710
multiply five by the whole
number three to get to 15.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:07.963
So I like this choice.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:11.860
Five is a factor of 15.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:14.010
Well, a factor, factors of a number

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.580
are numbers that you can multiply together

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.950
to get that number.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.600
So five is a factor of 15,
and three is a factor of 15,

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.800
because five times three is 15.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.380
So this one is also true.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:26.220
It would've also been true

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.890
if they'd said three is a factor of 15,

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:30.130
or if they'd said 15
is a multiple of five.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:32.210
Any of those would have
been true statements

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:36.693
based on what we know, that
five times three is equal to 15.

